course: biology
lesson: 325
title: Choosing a pet: the questions to ask first
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pet is not a present that ends after the birthday party. It is a living animal that needs food, care, company and a vet for many years, often for most of your school life and beyond.
explain: Wise families sit down before getting a pet and write a list: who feeds it, who cleans up, who walks it, where it goes on holiday, how long it is alone and how much it all costs.
explain: Picture a boy who dreams of a husky in a small flat while everyone is out all day. A husky was bred to pull sleds for hours in the snow, so it would be bored and lonely there; a pair of guinea pigs or some fish might fit his life far better.
explain: The right pet fits the home and the family's life, not just a cute video. Wild animals like monkeys do not belong in homes, and a puppy should be met with its mother, or found at a rescue centre.
fact: A dog usually lives about 10 to 13 years and a cat about 12 to 18, so a pet is a promise for many years.
fact: Before getting a pet, a family should agree who feeds it, cleans up, walks it, looks after it on holiday and pays for it; skipping these questions is why many animals end up in rescue centres.
fact: Dogs are pack animals and should not be left alone for more than about four hours; some dogs left too long bark, howl or chew out of worry.
fact: Pet allergies come from tiny bits of skin and spit, not really from fur, and no breed is truly allergy-free, so spending time with a pet first is a good test.
fact: Big, energetic dogs like huskies need lots of space and hours of running every day; a husky was bred to pull sleds for hours in the cold.
fact: Rescue centres take in lost or given-up animals, and staff help match each one to the right family; many older animals are already trained and calm.
fact: Guinea pigs, rabbits, rats and budgies are social and get lonely alone; guinea pigs have no tail you can see, and Switzerland has a law saying guinea pigs must be kept with a companion.
fact: Food, vet visits, vaccines, insurance, toys and beds cost far more than the pet itself, and over its life a dog can cost many thousands of pounds.
fact: Hamsters are night animals that sleep in the day and may bite if woken, and a fall from a small child's hands can badly hurt one.
fact: Monkeys and other wild animals need groups, space and food a home cannot give, often become unhappy and bite, and in many countries keeping them as pets is banned or strictly controlled.
fact: Some cheap puppies come from puppy farms where mothers are kept in poor conditions, and such puppies are more often ill or scared; good breeders and rescues let you meet the puppy with its mother.
exercise: About how long does a dog usually live? | About 10 to 13 years | About 1 or 2 years only | About 50 years | About 6 months
exercise: About how long does a cat usually live? | About 12 to 18 years | About 3 years | About 80 years, longer than a person | About one summer
exercise: Which question should a family answer before getting a pet? | Who will feed it, clean up and pay for it | What it will be called on Instagram and TikTok | Which colour collar looks best | How fast it can run
exercise: Why should a dog not be left alone all day? | Dogs are pack animals and get lonely and worried | Dogs sleep much better when the whole house is empty and quiet | Dogs need quiet to grow | Dogs only wake up at night
exercise: About how long at most should a dog be left alone? | About four hours | About two whole days | A whole week or more | About ten minutes
exercise: What really causes most pet allergies? | Tiny bits of skin and spit | Only long fur, never short fur | The pet's new leather collar | The pet's plastic food bowl
exercise: Is any dog or cat breed truly allergy-free? | No, none is truly allergy-free | Yes, all small dogs are | Yes, all white cats are | Yes, any pet with short fur
exercise: What was a husky bred to do? | Pull sleds for hours in the cold | Sit quietly on a sofa all day long | Guard the goldfish in a garden pond | Swim in warm tropical seas to catch fish
exercise: Why might a rescue animal be a good first pet? | Staff know it well and many older ones are trained and calm | Rescue animals have already had their jabs, so they never need a vet again | Rescue animals live for ever | Rescue animals need no food
exercise: Why should a guinea pig not live alone? | Guinea pigs are social and get lonely | Guinea pigs fight when kept in pairs | Guinea pigs prefer cats as friends | A single guinea pig grows too fat to move
exercise: Which country has a law that guinea pigs must have a companion? | Switzerland | The United States | South Africa | The Netherlands
exercise: What costs the most over a dog's life? | Food, vets, vaccines and insurance | The price paid for the puppy | Only the lead and collar | Nothing, dogs are free after you buy them
exercise: Why is a hamster a poor choice for a small child who wants to cuddle? | It sleeps by day, may bite if woken and can be hurt by a fall | It sleeps all night and plays all morning, when the child is at school | It is too big to hold | It hates being fed
exercise: Why should a monkey not be kept as a pet? | It needs a group, space and food a home cannot give | It cannot climb in a house, because the walls are too smooth | It is too small to see | It only eats chocolate
exercise: What is a good sign when buying a puppy? | You can meet the puppy with its mother | It is the cheapest one online | It is delivered in a van to a car park | The seller will not show the home
test: «it's my birthday, just want a puppy for like a year» What is the best reply? | A dog usually lives 10 to 13 years, so it is a promise for many years | Fine, after a year you can just take it back to the shop you got it from | Fine, puppies stay small for one year | Puppies only live for a year anyway
test: Count them: a family has 2 dogs, 1 cat and 3 guinea pigs. How many legs and tails in all? | 24 legs and 3 tails | 24 legs and 6 tails | 12 legs and 6 tails | 18 legs and 3 tails
test: Count them: 2 budgies and 2 rabbits live together. How many legs and how many long ears? | 12 legs and 4 long ears | 16 legs and 8 long ears | 8 legs and 4 long ears | 12 legs and 8 long ears
test: «whole family's out from 8 till 6, still want a dog tho» Which pet would suit better? | Fish or a pair of guinea pigs that cope with the day alone | A big husky that needs hours of running | A puppy that needs a wee break every few hours | A monkey that needs a whole group
test: «my cousin's dog is hypoallergenic so I won't sneeze, right» What is the truth? | No breed is truly allergy-free; spend time with it first to test | Right, allergies come only from cats, so any dog at all is completely safe | Right, those dogs have no skin | Right, but only if it is a puppy
test: In a cartoon a girl wins a puppy at a fair and that is the whole story. What is missing? | Who feeds, walks and pays for it for many years | The puppy's name tag and a shiny new collar | A bigger prize | The fair ticket
test: «just one guinea pig, it'll have me» What is the best reply? | Guinea pigs need one of their own kind to play and talk with | One is best, because two guinea pigs in a cage always fight | One is fine, they hate company | Guinea pigs only need a mirror
test: «puppy's only 50 quid online, sorted» Why be careful? | Cheap puppies may come from puppy farms and be ill or scared | Cheap puppies are always the healthiest, because they eat the least food | Price shows how clever a puppy is | Online puppies never need vaccines
test: A boy sees a cute video of a pet monkey in a nappy. What is the video not showing? | Monkeys often become unhappy, bite and need groups and space | Monkeys love nappies more than trees | Monkeys need nothing but bananas | Monkeys become calmer every year at home
test: Why might a hairless cat still make someone sneeze? | Allergies come from skin and spit, which it still has | Hairless cats sneeze on people, and the sneeze spreads to them | Hairless cats are made of fur inside | It cannot; hairless cats are always safe
test: What would happen if families never asked the questions before getting a pet? | More animals would end up given away to rescue centres | Every pet would be perfectly cared for | Pets would choose their own families | Vets would become free
exam: Identify the principal consideration that ought to precede the acquisition of a domestic animal. | Responsibility for its feeding, care and expense over many years | The selection of an appropriate name, collar and bed before its arrival | The maximum speed at which the animal is able to run across open ground | The popularity of the chosen breed upon the various social media
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning allergy to domestic animals. | It arises from skin and saliva, and no breed is entirely free of it | It is caused principally by the food and treats which the animal consumes | It is prevented entirely by the selection of a short-haired breed of animal | It is caused chiefly by the leather collar worn about the animal's neck
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the keeping of guinea pigs in Switzerland? | The law requires that a guinea pig be kept with a companion | The law prohibits the keeping of guinea pigs | The law requires that a guinea pig be kept alone | The law requires that a guinea pig be walked daily
exam: Ascertain which of the following constitutes a favourable indication when acquiring a puppy. | The prospective owner is permitted to observe the puppy together with its mother | The puppy is offered at the lowest available price on the internet | The puppy is delivered to a car park without inspection | The seller declines to disclose the premises
